{title: Peace, Perfect Peace}
{artist: Edward H. Bickersteth / George T. Caldbeck}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Meditative}
{key: C}
{tempo: 115}
{time: 4/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (The Hymnbook (Richmond, Virginia: Presbyterian Church in the United States, 1955), # 420)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]Peace, [G7]perfect [C]peace, in [F]this [Dm]dark world [G7]of [C]sin?
[C]The [F]blood [Ab7]of [C]Jesus whis[F]pers [C]peace__[G7]__ wit[C]hin.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]Peace, [G7]perfect [C]peace, by [F]throng[Dm]ing du[G7]ties [C]pressed?
[C]To [F]do [Ab7]the [C]will of Je[F]sus, [C]this__[G7]__ is [C]rest.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]Peace, [G7]perfect [C]peace, with [F]sor[Dm]rows surg[G7]ing [C]round?
[C]On [F]Je[Ab7]sus’ [C]bosom naught [F]but [C]calm__[G7]__ is [C]found.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[C]Peace, [G7]perfect [C]peace, with [F]loved [Dm]ones far [G7]a[C]way?
[C]In [F]Je[Ab7]sus’ [C]keeping we [F]are [C]safe,__[G7]__ and [C]they.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[C]Peace, [G7]perfect [C]peace, our [F]fu[Dm]ture all [G7]un[C]known?
[C]Je[F]sus [Ab7]we [C]know, and He [F]is [C]on__[G7]__ the [C]throne.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 7}
[C]It [G7]is e[C]nough: earth’s [F]strug[Dm]gles soon [G7]shall [C]cease,
[C]And [F]Je[Ab7]sus [C]call us to [F]Heaven’s [C]per__[G7]__fect [C]peace.
{end_of_verse}
